On moving from left to right in a period, ionisation energy increases. Thus, correct order of ionisation energy of $C, N, O, F$ should be

\mathrm{C} < \mathrm{N} < \mathrm{O} < \mathrm{F}

But the ionisation energy of $\mathrm{N}$ is found to be greater than that of O. This is due to the presence of half-filled p-orbitals in $\mathrm{N}$ which provide it extra stability. Thus, the correct order is $\mathrm{C} \lt  \mathrm{O} \lt  \mathrm{N} \lt  \mathrm{F}$.

